  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_0e33afb908764a608bf726b9fe61c21a",
      "statement": "`.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml` refreshes this repository's own `openwiki/` wiki by invoking the OpenWiki CLI directly on a GitHub-hosted runner, with no API, queue or worker pool — a separate path from the `openwiki-service` product in `app/`, which generates wikis through a SQLite queue and worker containers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L12-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c3314efc218917f41c8acb9e037f496a7fd2168d10c0402d3a159e2643ae4aa9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L9-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bde427a81803e461c3afe7247a748f69111b73df6086715fb0724e1903661a59:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d616bd8dc0944343ab561cdab6fc009a",
      "statement": "The refresh workflow runs on a daily `schedule` (`cron: \"0 8 * * *\"`) and on manual `workflow_dispatch`, and requests the two write scopes its steps need: `contents: write` for pushing the update branch and `pull-requests: write` for creating the pull request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L3-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93ca2da0784da6a240c06dd9c7978af1d1ef0d2fc3b690d5450837641e49ad3c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_98ddbb54c83948c1ad8a39811bcf0919",
      "statement": "The CLI step runs `openwiki code --update --print` with `continue-on-error: true`, so the run-state cleanup and the pull-request step still execute after a failed generation; the failure is re-raised only by the final `Propagate OpenWiki failure` step, which runs `exit 1` when `steps.openwiki.outcome == 'failure'`, making a failed generation a red workflow run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L33-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d58ef5f498c02b45776d67452c92ddb307313815a56beddaf62b0c62e897fa58:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L80-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fd6f0cbd8d9f20e4111509ed1d7e17265ef0726a5b025ee59f6b717d085a3a96:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8cb4407b8a1c430eaa28d249896f66ff",
      "statement": "The checkout step requires `fetch-depth: 0` because `--update` diffs current `HEAD` against the commit recorded in `openwiki/.last-update.json`; a shallow clone does not contain that commit, so the update would run against an empty change summary. This is the CI counterpart of `ingestion.ensure_full_history`, which unshallows a clone with `git fetch --unshallow` before an `update` run for the same reason.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L16-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f513af748b362994b00e41cc2ab8ac7880f4f9a4ac3fb63f49be6f3f2680e8b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/ingestion.py#L209-L226",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cd81cb938ad3fc8663b62b4cd7acf922a4936bea7ca0380d6a52cefa24a41b49:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9af1db6579014b10bfac01c736886def",
      "statement": "The workflow pins the toolchain exactly: Node.js 22 via `actions/setup-node` (the same major the Docker image sets as `NODE_MAJOR=22`) and `npm install --global openwiki@0.6.0` together with the optional `mermaid` and `jsdom` packages that add high-fidelity validation of Mermaid diagrams.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L24-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20dbe255a504d02044dd17679a961cfec4a69d2a04cbfe3d13adacde576d6f8c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile#L9-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33eec4774ffd95297caa2f2fc62753b874dd0b1c8855c22c4efe78c798f573fd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_036f48da82b04a1c9fa1156557695309",
      "statement": "The workflow pins the OpenWiki CLI version separately from the service image: the workflow installs `openwiki@0.6.0` from npm while `Dockerfile` defaults `OPENWIKI_VERSION=0.6.0` and passes it to `scripts/install-openwiki.sh`, which installs it globally with `npm install --global openwiki@${VERSION}`; upgrading OpenWiki therefore requires changing both pins or they drift.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L29-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7232df229782005627e77c69977780972255cb721ca43928bef49c5b5b379526:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile#L22-L25",
