          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49ea2f33c70f2230ba00a64bd8485003dcfbdeabd6de107dad0248c0643aad78:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53e20186fc5a4ac7af2b94de72ec1413",
      "statement": "Model-provider configuration for the CI run lives in the CLI step's `env`: `OPENWIKI_PROVIDER=openrouter`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` from the `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` secret, `OPENWIKI_MODEL_ID=deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash`, and `OPENWIKI_LANGSMITH_API_KEY` (required for the LangSmith connector's code-mode pull to authenticate, with extra workspaces added as `OPENWIKI_LANGSMITH_API_KEY_2`, `_3`, … secrets); `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`, `LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=openwiki` and `LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true` are optional and trace the workflow's own run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L33-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:472e728f3a1262f429bf64fd0d40715ba30236e99e4c400fa0049932a52fe277:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9a0d411e4b2547c1b46dbc6ca4bad59a",
      "statement": "A dedicated step runs `rm -f -- openwiki/.run.json` under `if: ${{ !cancelled() }}` before the pull-request step, because `create-pull-request` commits whatever the `add-paths` whitelist matches (there is no git pathspec exclusion) and the transient resume state must not reach the branch; the same exclusion is enforced in the service by the pathspec `:(exclude)<artifact_dir>/.run.json` and asserted by `tests/test_push.py`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L50-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5755853ba18a4732efe67aeac152e11ab7c085d7401d799bf5d8ee495f350e9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/publisher.py#L39-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fb1c17315d5bff9e151ff88393d0f62c634e23ab581fcc7194495c5b0d2f4d99:"
        },
        {
