        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c92e10cfe6e24869bb66028cbdc646d9",
      "statement": "The pull request is scoped to exactly four paths — `openwiki`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml` — on the fixed branch `openwiki/update` with commit message and title `docs: update OpenWiki`, so unrelated working-tree changes cannot leak into the PR and successive runs converge on the same branch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L54-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83e7c079f8ea862748e99e8fc56dd07e8fec5fc78f7843362dc0439bbd1b777d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_433e9fe62eb14a629ffe1ad58df7791e",
      "statement": "The workflow treats a failed generation as mergeable partial progress: both the cleanup step and the PR step are guarded by `if: ${{ !cancelled() }}`, the PR body echoes `${{ steps.openwiki.outcome }}` and states that on `failure` the PR intentionally preserves only the pages completed before the failure and that merging it makes that progress the baseline for the next scheduled run, while an annotation step emits a `::notice` with the PR URL only when `steps.create-pr.outputs.pull-request-url` is non-empty.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L50-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a839067f47beb1ca08c710b71e598b0402cc1fd184fbaffb0641be925ef8a7a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L67-L78",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:94152a5d780749f4af7c60e590acea59708af2fe80434980b63e3cf8a6c3eb04:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ebba6db0cdec4ac5aab8faced808c13d",
      "statement": "`AGENTS.md` is the OpenWiki-owned scaffolding: it declares that the generated `openwiki/` tree is optional just-in-time context rather than required startup reading, tells agents to treat source code and tests as authoritative, and instructs not to hand-edit generated OpenWiki pages — preferring source/doc updates and regeneration by the scheduled workflow — with all of that inside the `<!-- OPENWIKI:START -->`/`<!-- OPENWIKI:END -->` markers that the workflow is allowed to rewrite.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/openwiki-update.yml#L58-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cd0f5c60b0d28d80cb6273529693534dd71f8dd916ccbfbc05e4973346ad444c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L1-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8926524de63a1266e7592d9f1256ec367b67e9fa0583f343808e3e51f19d4990:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a9c462236bb34b04b5e004ef00402f0a",
      "statement": "`CLAUDE.md` contains nothing but `@AGENTS.md` inside the same `OPENWIKI:START`/`OPENWIKI:END` markers, so Claude Code inherits the AGENTS.md block instead of duplicating it while the file stays under OpenWiki's ownership.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L1-L7",
